      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n#include <omp.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\n/*\n * Compute the gravitational impact among all pairs of bodies in \n * the system.\n */\nvoid body_force(float * restrict X, float * restrict Y, float * restrict Z,\n                float * restrict VX, float * restrict VY, float * restrict VZ,\n                float dt, int n) {\n  #pragma omp for simd schedule(static)\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n    float xi = X[i];\n    float yi = Y[i];\n    float zi = Z[i];\n    float fx = 0.0f;\n    float fy = 0.0f;\n    float fz = 0.0f;\n\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n      float dx = X[j] - xi;\n      float dy = Y[j] - yi;\n      float dz = Z[j] - zi;\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n      float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n      fx += dx * inv_dist3;\n      fy += dy * inv_dist3;\n      fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n    }\n\n    VX[i] += dt*fx;\n    VY[i] += dt*fy;\n    VZ[i] += dt*fz;\n  }\n}\n\n/*\n * Read a binary dataset with initialized bodies.\n */\nvoid read_dataset(int *nbodies, float **X, float **Y, float **Z,\n                  float **VX, float **VY, float **VZ) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  int n = *nbodies;\n  float *tmp = (float *)malloc((size_t)n * 6 * sizeof(float));\n  b = fread(tmp, (size_t)n * 6 * sizeof(float), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  *X = (float *)malloc((size_t)n * sizeof(float));\n  *Y = (float *)malloc((size_t)n * sizeof(float));\n  *Z = (float *)malloc((size_t)n * sizeof(float));\n  *VX = (float *)malloc((size_t)n * sizeof(float));\n  *VY = (float *)malloc((size_t)n * sizeof(float));\n  *VZ = (float *)malloc((size_t)n * sizeof(float));\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n    (*X)[i] = tmp[6*i + 0];\n    (*Y)[i] = tmp[6*i + 1];\n    (*Z)[i] = tmp[6*i + 2];\n    (*VX)[i] = tmp[6*i + 3];\n    (*VY)[i] = tmp[6*i + 4];\n    (*VZ)[i] = tmp[6*i + 5];\n  }\n  free(tmp);\n}\n\n/*\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\n */\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, float *X, float *Y, float *Z,\n                   float *VX, float *VY, float *VZ) {\n  float *tmp = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * 6 * sizeof(float));\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n    tmp[6*i + 0] = X[i];\n    tmp[6*i + 1] = Y[i];\n    tmp[6*i + 2] = Z[i];\n    tmp[6*i + 3] = VX[i];\n    tmp[6*i + 4] = VY[i];\n    tmp[6*i + 5] = VZ[i];\n  }\n  int b = fwrite(tmp, (size_t)nbodies * 6 * sizeof(float), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  free(tmp);\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n  float *X, *Y, *Z, *VX, *VY, *VZ;\n\n  read_dataset(&nbodies, &X, &Y, &Z, &VX, &VY, &VZ);\n\n  #pragma omp parallel\n  {\n    for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n      body_force(X, Y, Z, VX, VY, VZ, DT, nbodies);\n      // implicit barrier after worksharing loop\n\n      #pragma omp for simd schedule(static)\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        X[i] += VX[i] * DT;\n        Y[i] += VY[i] * DT;\n        Z[i] += VZ[i] * DT;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, X, Y, Z, VX, VY, VZ);\n\n  free(X); free(Y); free(Z);\n  free(VX); free(VY); free(VZ);\n\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Converting the body data from Array-of-Structs to Struct-of-Arrays, moving the OpenMP parallel region outside the time-step loop, and using combined worksharing-SIMD constructs on both the force and position-update loops will improve performance beyond previous attempts. Each thread processes multiple bodies in SIMD lanes while keeping every body's inner j-reduction scalar, preserving exact floating-point results per body. The SoA layout improves memory locality for vector loads, and hoisting the parallel region eliminates repeated thread-team creation overhead.",
  "notes": "The transformation preserves bit-exact output because each i-th body's force reduction over j remains sequential; only the outer loop is distributed across threads/SIMD lanes. Input/output are converted to/from SoA once at start/end, which is negligible compared to simulation cost. The code uses restrict pointers and OpenMP 4+ combined worksharing-SIMD directives.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Convert Body array-of-structs to separate float arrays (SoA) for x,y,z,vx,vy,vz",
    "Move #pragma omp parallel outside the time-step loop and use worksharing constructs inside",
    "Use #pragma omp for simd on both force and position-update loops to enable SIMD across bodies per thread"
  ]
